/-!
# Genuine native period classes on arbitrary original base opens

For each actual base open, genuine exact open restriction and the
proved original restriction biholomorphism identify the original total
holomorphic sheaf's cohomology-presheaf value on its full preimage with
genuine cohomology of the original restricted period family, in every
degree. Both original complex atlas constructions are retained.

Four holomorphic functions on the base open therefore define an actual
neighborhood extension class. Its comparison is precisely the original
restricted-family period cocycle class. Actual holomorphic complex-linear
period characters vanish. The comparison and class construction preserve
the original scalar maps, and the module structures are independently
induced by the actual sheaf scalar endomorphisms and native Ext functors.
Two holomorphic functions also give such a genuine complex-linear class
map by inserting the first two marked coefficients.

The existing biholomorphic cohomology comparison requires a Hausdorff
source; it is supplied by Hausdorffness of the original base. No source
compactness or finite-dimensionality is assumed. The construction here
is objectwise on every base open: it does not assert compatibility of
classes across different base opens, a sheaf frame, or a higher-direct-image
isomorphism.
-/
